        "payload": "tree fe4fea8a23983a2b8b982e8508035efbcb4676f3\nparent 9bf4815b94b9eaf8807f4e569091778da6c338d5\nauthor optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1793622707 +0100\ncommitter optout21 <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com> 1793622822 +0100\n\ntest: p2p: check v1 magic bytes only after the full header\n\nThe v1 message parser in P2PConnection rejected the stream as soon as\nthe first 4 bytes did not match the network magic. bitcoind's\nV1Transport::readHeader waits for the full 24-byte header before\nchecking the magic.\n\nThe v2 to v1 downgrade relies on bitcoind's behaviour: an outbound v2\nconnection is only retried with v1 (V2Transport::ShouldReconnectV1)\nif at least a v1 header's worth of bytes had been sent before the\npeer disconnected. If the node's first send reaches the test peer in\nsmall pieces, the Python peer could disconnect after just 4 bytes, the\nnode would not retry with v1, and p2p_v2_encrypted.py would time out\nwaiting for the reconnection.\n\nMatch bitcoind by checking the magic only once the full header has\nbeen received.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCgAdFiEEmuHXOVRjWiwQgEZAHancOgcdFYIFAmrog0UACgkQHancOgcd\nFYL6tAv/aYNWloTGIPkPLgXo+J+iELQWZ+4dMuYDQ4idVO6JoHGorZhK2bkToFRA\nFbXhUsRHLaI1zeP2/wC/gGy2v41NMq6cXJ5bJ/9YJgSdP56NxdPdivWWKgeMkeQ9\nuK159OwBGGDPD/SGFbBlRyqoYfDEaSzrvjKMYrmhSQMNwOxzh3IMZSkHyyrehDBO\nsF3+ULRCJr1aYfhyvkBa43AyW8ZPZ3XdT+zueEOimP1DHOWLm/dpQ9WLR3AjDc+D\nOoZgHDMmRwc1rQgXrZdIhEjTdw8jb+Ea31U07hwypSgP2ryHFwAX5BCdaQyJTeQ9\n8PuKeabcsIzANlqbG1tlEKX+6Gdzk6jPZ+SO96N99ksMwB0PTjszXd36CND3hhsG\nUN3IW+TiW4I1/VDz/f9QuL/u1yyjZ4EjWthZmOi3LUNJhGhEXvhIuhdt6/qVfnSW\nSAPcX6/7nilDlnvPzx23lgD1ALquCNnqw1u1XlUFEJskHaPYYZNhVYxKv5WAJJBP\nlcwOrAaa\n=lKms\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
